---
title: How to setup availability for meeting booking form
sidebar:
  order: 2
---
Define specific time slots and available days for booking meetings.

### **Steps to Set Up Availability:**

1. **Navigate to Availability Tab:**

   - In the meeting settings, click on the ‘Availability’ tab.

1. **Select Available Date Range:**

   - Choose the date range during which bookings will be available.

1. **Enable Days for Booking:**

   - Toggle the switch next to each day (e.g., **Sunday**, **Monday**) to enable or disable availability for that day.

1. **Add Time Slots:**

   - Click on the ‘**+ Add Time Slot’** button.
   - In the pop-up window, select the **Start Time** and **End Time**.
   - Click ‘**Add Slot**’ to save the time slot.

1. **Delete Time Slots (Optional):**

   - Click on the **Trash Icon** next to an existing time slot to remove it.

1. **Save Changes:**

   - Once your availability is configured, it will be save automatically.

![](./how-to-setup-availability-for-meeting-booking-form/content/image-12.png)

### **Best Practices:**

- Add multiple time slots to accommodate varying schedules.
- Regularly review availability settings to ensure accuracy.
- Avoid overlapping time slots.

**That’s it! Your meeting availability is now set up and ready for booking.**
